mmary of what it does:\n\n## Regex Explanation\n\nThe regex in `/app/regex.txt` matches **the last YYYY-MM-DD date on lines containing a valid IPv4 address**.\n\n### Key Components:\n\n1. **IPv4 Pattern**: `(?:0|[1-9]\\d?|1\\d{2}|2[0-4]\\d|25[0-5])\\.(...)`\n   - Matches octets 0-255 without leading zeros\n   - Example: `192.168.1.1` ✓ but `192.168.01.1` ✗\n\n2. **Date Pattern with Month/Day Validation**:\n   - **February**: 01-29 days\n   - **April, June, September, November**: 01-30 days  \n   - **All other months**: 01-31 days\n   - Example: `2023-02-29` ✓, `2023-02-30` ✗, `2023-04-31` ✗\n\n3. **Word Boundaries**: `(?<!\\w)` and `(?!\\w)`\n   - Prevents false matches like `1134-12-1234`\n   - Ensures dates/IPs aren't part of longer alphanumeric sequences\n\n4. **Last Date Selection**: `(?!.*(?<!\\w)\\d{4}-...)` \n   - Negative lookahead ensures no additional dates follow\n   - Returns only the final date on each line\n\n### Test Results: ✓ All 15 tests pass\n\nThe regex correctly:\n- Extracts dates only from lines with IPv4 addresses\n- Returns only the last date when multiple exist\n- Rejects invalid date combinations (Feb 30, Apr 31, etc.)\n- Avoids false positives (numbers, leading zeros, malformed dates)","ttft_ms":141286,"type":"result","duration_ms":272359,"uuid":"6e74c33e-f827-480a-b405-08e5b9ab31dd","ttft_stream_ms":934,"time_to_request_ms":70,"queued_turn_count":0}
